It has nothing to do with formatR, because it does not work even with<br>tidy=FALSE. I do not know the real reason either, but you can<br>certainly use cat(..., sep = &#39;&#39;) (the default value of sep is a<br>space), e.g.<br><br>cat(&quot;Percent simulation error based on actual answer 244/495 is &quot;,<br>      Error, &quot;%.&quot;, &quot;
&quot;, sep = &quot;&quot;)<br><br><br>Regards,<br>Yihui<br>--<br>Yihui Xie &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">xiey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>Phone: <a href="tel:(515)%20294-2465" value="+15152942465" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">515-294-2465</a> Web: <a href="http://yihui.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355995830000&amp;usg=AOvVaw18IV82LU_LxFk0Pd2-cW9M">http://yihui.name</a><br>Department of Statistics, Iowa State University<br>2215 Snedecor Hall, Ames, IA<br><br><br>On Sun, Dec 23, 2012 at 4:27 PM, Alan &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">arnh...@appstate.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; \documentclass{article}<br>&gt; \usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}<br>&gt;<br>&gt;  egin{document}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Problem is when I use<br>&gt;  egin{verbatim}<br>&gt; cat(&quot;Percent simulation error based on actual answer 244/495 is&quot;,<br>&gt;       Error,&quot; %.&quot;, &quot;
&quot;)<br>&gt; \end{verbatim}<br>&gt; in the code below a strange character is inserted (presumably from<br>&gt; formatR?)...In the code below, I avoid the problem by running:<br>&gt;  egin{verbatim}<br>&gt; cat(&quot;Percent simulation error based on actual answer 244/495 is&quot;,<br>&gt;       Error,&quot;%.&quot;, &quot;
&quot;)<br>&gt; \end{verbatim}<br>&gt; But, this of course has a space between the number and the percent symbol.<br>&gt; Any suggestions or workarounds much appreciated. Alan<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &lt;&lt;c01SIMcraps, comment = NA&gt;&gt;=<br>&gt; SIMcraps &lt;- function(n.games = 10000){<br>&gt;   options(scipen=999)  # Suppress scientific notation in the output<br>&gt;   # linebet returns 0 or 1 based on whether &#39;shooter&#39; loses or wins<br>&gt;   linebet &lt;- function(){<br>&gt;     comeoutroll &lt;- sum(sample(1:6, 2, replace = TRUE))  # first throw<br>&gt;     if (comeoutroll %in% c(7, 11)){<br>&gt;       result &lt;- 1 # win<br>&gt;     } else if (comeoutroll %in% c(2, 3, 12)) {<br>&gt;       result &lt;- 0 # loss<br>&gt;     } else {<br>&gt;       breakvalue &lt;- 0<br>&gt;       repeat{<br>&gt;         substhrow &lt;- sum(sample(1:6, 2, replace = TRUE))<br>&gt;         # subsequent throw<br>&gt;         if(substhrow == comeoutroll){<br>&gt;           result &lt;- 1 # win<br>&gt;           breakvalue &lt;- 1<br>&gt;         } else if (substhrow == 7){<br>&gt;           result &lt;- 0 # loss<br>&gt;           breakvalue &lt;- 1<br>&gt;         }<br>&gt;         if(breakvalue == 1) break<br>&gt;       }<br>&gt;     }<br>&gt;     result<br>&gt;   }<br>&gt;   gameOutcome &lt;- numeric(n.games)  # vector of 0s of length n.games<br>&gt;   # Play n.games simulated crap games<br>&gt;   for(i in 1:n.games){gameOutcome[i] &lt;- linebet()}<br>&gt;   # gameOutcomes is a vector of wins and losses<br>&gt;   P.win &lt;- mean(gameOutcome)       # Percent of time shooter wins<br>&gt;   Actual.answer &lt;- 244/495<br>&gt;   Error &lt;- round(abs(Actual.answer - P.win)/Actual.answer * 100, 4)<br>&gt;   cat(&quot;Simulated probability of winning =&quot;,  P.win, &quot;based on&quot;,<br>&gt;       n.games, &quot;simulated games.&quot;, &quot;
&quot;)<br>&gt;   cat(&quot;Percent simulation error based on actual answer 244/495 is&quot;,<br>&gt;       Error,&quot;%.&quot;, &quot;
&quot;)<br>&gt; }<br>&gt; @<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Running the function:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; &lt;&lt;c01Simcraps2, comment = NA&gt;&gt;=<br>&gt; SIMcraps(n.games = 50000)<br>&gt; @<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; \end{document}<br>
